Single-database configuration for Flask, via Flask-Migrate (Alembic).

Schema changes go through Alembic now - the old migrate_add_*.py
standalone scripts are gone. Workflow for a new schema change:

1. Edit models.py.
2. Generate a migration (autogenerate diffs models.py against the DB
   pointed to by DATABASE_URL):
       flask db migrate -m "add whatever"
3. Read the generated file in migrations/versions/ - autogenerate is a
   starting point, not gospel (it misses some renames/defaults).
4. Apply it locally and confirm the app still works:
       flask db upgrade
5. Commit the migration file, push, then run the same `flask db upgrade`
   against prod (e.g. via Render's Shell tab, where DATABASE_URL is
   already set) before/alongside the deploy that needs the new column -
   otherwise requests touching it will fail until it's run.

versions/0001-0011 reconstruct the schema evolution that used to live in
migrate_add_*.py scripts (see each file's docstring for which script it
replaces). Prod was brought under Alembic via `flask db stamp head`, not
`upgrade` - the schema already existed, stamp just recorded that fact in
alembic_version without re-running any DDL.
